Instead of writing yath 2.0 from scratch, we are going to start with 1.0 as a base and modify it into what we want.

Broad strokes:
 * Mechanical rename of App::Yath namespace to App::Yath2
 * Mechanical rename of Test2::Harness namespace to Test2::Harness2
 * Mechanical change of all version numbers to 2.000000
 * Implement App::Yath::Script::V2 so the `yath` script can use the 2.0 we are writing
 * Migration to Getopt::Yath for argument processing
 * Switch to using Test2-Collector for executing and auditing tests, witht he current yath collector being simplified to gather events from the .jsonl.zst files the collector writes instead of gathering raw events and parsing/auditing them
 * Use collectors for all processes involved in yath, not just tests
 * Move to only pipelining transitions instead of sending all events everywhere
  * Will need state sync similar to the 'Monitor' work we did in the `2.0b` branch, or one of its worktrees
  * Renderer rewrite so that base renderer (or renderer role) knows how to find the .jsonl.zst files
 * Implementation of the system load service (we implemented a version of this in a 2.0 branch or worktree)
  * Ability to gate number of tests run concurrently on cpu/mem usage in addition to, or instead of a static -j value
 * rewrite the DB+UI layer that is currently Test2-Harness-UI, but write it inline.

So architectural changes:
 * Getopt::Yath
 * Test2-Collector

For now Test2-Collector is not installed, and I am not ready to install it, it
still needs review. But it is symlinked as ./t2clib/ so we can already access
it.

We will be migrating things in small chunks to try to get to the following architecture:

 * One main harness service that does scheduling and job dispatch, and hold the canonical state
 * Collectors for all processes including main harness
 * Collectors report transitions to main harness
 * Other things that need transitions get them from the main harness
 * Things that need more complete events (not just transitions) directly seek
   out the .jsonl.zst files instead of all events going through pipe to
   everything.
 * Any non-test, non-spawn process started by yath will be wrapped in a
   collector, any that need to receive and handle requests will get a unix
   socket, others such as the system load service which do not recieve
   requests, but only send state changes when the system load changes, will
   connect to the main harnesses socket instead of having their own.
 * Log files will be sqlite databases with the events.jsonl.zst files stored in the artifacts tables

When we do get to the database layer we will use DBIx::QuickORM.


Several branches and worktrees that we have abandonded implemented parts of this, but always from scratch. We may reference those for architectural info moving forward.


